The average height (or average heel height in this case) would be calculated by attempting to reduce every instance of measurement to a single, centrally-located number. Since we have a mixture of heel heights, we can determine the average as follows. First, multiply the number of women wearing 4 inch heels by the heel height: (3 women * 4 inches/woman) = 12 inches. Second, multiply the number of women wearing 2 inch heels by the heel height: (3 women * 2 inches/woman) = 6 inches. Third, add these products together: 12 inches + 6 inches = 18 inches. Fourth, divide this sum by the total number of women, which is 6: 18 inches / 6 women = 3 inches/woman.

\boxed{3}

